rustix's libc back end on Radix: mlibc has statvfs but no statfs,
no fallocate modes and no IPPROTO_MPTCP; ioctl request numbers are
unsigned long, as on the BSDs, and msg_controllen is a socklen_t, as
POSIX has it. Its struct termios is Linux's, with c_line: without it,
tcgetattr wrote past the end of rustix's Termios and the special codes
were one place off, so crossterm's raw mode never set VMIN.

